# Task 148-018 Execution Plan: i18n Parity — TR/EN Task Description Routing Identical

## Goal
Verify that the same semantic tasks described in TR and EN produce identical routing decisions
(primary intent + agent selection) from the classifyIntent() + routing engine.

## Approach
1. Import classifyIntent() from src/core/intent-classifier.ts
2. Import AGENT_FALLBACK_CHAIN + selectAgentByFallback from src/core/routing-engine.ts
3. Define 4 TR/EN task pairs with identical scope but different language descriptions
4. For each pair, verify primary intent and agent selection match
5. Assert 8 tests total (4 pairs × 2 assertions each)

## Key insight
The intent classifier uses .toLowerCase() which handles ASCII but not Turkish characters.
Turkish has special case rules (I→ı, İ→i). However, the INTENT_KEYWORDS are all ASCII English.
TR tasks will still match keywords because keywords are matched against the text.
The scope-based signals (scope directories) are identical for TR/EN pairs.
Therefore routing should be identical — scope dominates over text keywords.

